@description ReaPackLab: centrally managed REAPER package manager
@author ReaLab
@version 0.14.4
@changelog
  Temporary classroom recovery: retrieve one-line HTTPS configuration pointer from ReaPackLab-Config/bootstrap-url.txt.
  Ignore malformed local url.txt on standard macOS installations without requiring privileged file changes.
  Preserve strict INI validation, managed repository policy, and the current Setup 0.1.1 installer.
  macOS 15.0+ Apple Silicon (ARM64). Developer ID-signed; not notarized.
@provides
  [darwin-arm64] reaper_reapacklab-arm64.dylib https://github.com/rockumk/ReaPackLab/releases/download/v$version/$path
@link
  Distribution repository https://github.com/rockumk/ReaPackLab
  Source code https://github.com/rockumk/ReaPackLabDev
@about
  # ReaPackLab

  ReaPackLab is a fork of ReaPack designed for managed REAPER environments.

  This package provides a Developer ID-signed macOS 15.0+ Apple Silicon
  binary. It is the centrally managed edition, not the separate
  ReaPackLabSetup bootstrap extension. This release is not notarized. Use in a clean test REAPER
  installation before classroom deployment.

  Based on ReaPack by Christian Fillion (LGPL-3.0-or-later).
